The selector candidate remains unintegrated. Its fixed adversarial fallback p95 median is **27.91% slower than baseline**, with disjoint observed ranges: candidate 0.9251–1.4911 ms/call versus baseline 0.7436–0.8427. Against the original it is 26.93% slower by median, while those observed ranges overlap. Ordinary p95 is 78.13% faster than baseline by median and constructed p95 is 89.63% faster, with disjoint observed ranges, but these finite wins do not establish whole-candidate nonregression or universal superiority.

Small/large standard medians regress 5.18%/2.77% against baseline; all-percentiles/all-calculations medians regress 2.91%/0.61%. Those four ranges overlap. These are retained observed medians, not a statistical significance or durable-engine claim. Baseline already has a large advantage over original for all-percentiles/all-calculations, which must not be credited as a newly established selector improvement. [TABLES.md](TABLES.md) compares all three roles with medians/ranges. The complete source-bound values and per-repetition paired differences are in [recomputed-summary.json](recomputed-summary.json), [timing-summary.csv](timing-summary.csv), [memory-summary.csv](memory-summary.csv) and [paired-differences.csv](paired-differences.csv).

The measured candidate entry is SHA-256 `33574a99fd21029a7b564b1d9316c2b6d7389641c6b607d6bea61dc022457dd3`; its separately authenticated helper is `a6622d09853a8c1b550e6de919d0908a3647660bde561f250fcee9a81864763a`. Both exact modules are preserved under `preserved/study/`, along with baseline `9269cf8c32be9bf2c075b67019e82e41272d9495f0321fefc17b2c5695a91371`. They are retained rejected-study evidence, not a production proposal or accepted public application candidate. No production file, old source, trial, manifest, workload or threshold was edited. Standard/shared special/multi-selection/cache bodies remain the exact previously bound baseline bodies. Source layout and engine inlining remain hypotheses.

The independent original is the authenticated actual released @grafana/data 13.2.3 CJS reducer `36f6f81fc3ccc8708f8f42a306a0123b717d46320aa888df5acd0e0673514443`, using the actual resolved Lodash 4.17.23 source `71b4b7f5d2fc2d69399fd3edd7104fa10f9fd73fc600130825c3032ee8c50dad`. Consolidation reauthenticated all six loaded original files against the pinned registry archive members, SHA-512 registry integrity and SHA-256 identities; it also authenticated the Node executable and the eight preserved current Metrics production sources. No original reducer was invoked during consolidation. Original execution occurred only in the already authorized measurement/preflight workers. Application code invokes no original/vendor runtime.

The first measured controller receipt is `preserved/study/results/timing-attempt-1791843146474.json`; it authenticates `paired-control-1791843146458.json` and the raw controller stdout/stderr. Its 147 child records bind all 294 timing child stdout/stderr files. The memory receipt is `preserved/study/results/memory-observations-control-1791843441822.json`, SHA-256 `2c42b31e2c6768b2a4c5b6a4fc772d2674abc0c6e778bdc15cb2f61c94c98efd`. It binds all 147 child result/output hashes. Consolidation independently parsed their 588 child/observer raw logs, checked matching PIDs and checkpoint records, matched 1,979 observer samples and recomputed all peaks. Observer raw hashes were first recorded at consolidation; recorded sample counts/peaks and contents agree, but no earlier hash for each observer log existed in the original memory receipt.

There are 1,323 fresh/full-cache/subset packet checks in timing workers and 1,311,282 such checks in memory workers. All 147 timing and 147 memory children finished successfully, with no partial, failed, killed or limit-hit child. Timing results were independently recomputed and matched the original recorded summaries exactly. Memory summaries, lifetime/checkpoint/polled peaks, initialization/retention/release deltas and paired candidate-minus-reference values were independently computed from raw records. No negative value was clipped. Examples include candidate-minus-baseline retained-heap paired ranges of -72 to +72 bytes for small standard, -272 to +480 bytes for all calculations, and negative released-heap observations in both baseline and candidate all-calculations children. Small signed differences include GC variation and are not categorical allocator superiority evidence.

Timing controller execution was 22:10:46.412–22:12:26.476 UTC, **100.064 seconds**, against the prospective 3–5 minute reservation. Its inner paired controller interval was 22:10:46.462–22:12:26.458. Root authorized from 22:10:25 and explicitly closed at 22:12:39. Isolated memory was 22:12:56.918–22:17:21.822 UTC, **264.904 seconds**, against the 10–15 minute reservation. Root separately authorized it from 22:12:39 and explicitly closed at 22:17:32. Root and other agents reported no tests, builds, browser interactions, publication or source scans during these intervals. Unrelated Windows/background work was uncontrolled. [coordination.json](coordination.json) preserves the explicit authorization/close record and scope; it is an operational session record, not cryptographic attestation or a complete chat export.

Each timing child loads all three implementations for common correctness prevalidation; timing memory diagnostics are not isolated. Each memory child loads exactly one implementation—six original CJS files, one baseline module or two candidate modules. Native CJS caches were empty. Matching-PID observer data triggered its measurement-start handshake. Memory checkpoints and 100 ms polling can miss intermediate RSS peaks; the lifetime maxRSS metric is a complete-child high-water mark. Old-space 256 MiB and observed RSS 512 MiB are guardrails rather than OS memory isolation. The declared 120-second child limit and observer lifecycle remain unchanged. No aggregate memory-run deadline or atomic Windows process-tree/PID-reuse ownership is claimed.

After retained snapshots, each retained field is serialized and validated with two cached rereads before release/GC. That common pressure can affect released heap capacity and RSS. Signed deltas are diagnostic; no cumulative allocation, exact physical peak, leak proof, confidence interval, machine isolation or universal memory superiority is claimed. Higher candidate RSS medians in some standard/multi-selection cases are retained alongside lower p95 observations. The independent original/baseline references remain separate for every metric.

The full 117-file readiness inventory stayed unchanged. Its exact same source identities retain the historical 2,910,751 reducer comparisons, including 48,240 cache comparisons, plus 14,240 helper comparisons and held-out/adversarial controls. No full corpus replay was performed during these measured windows or consolidation. New measurement-stage readiness preserved the 42 adversarial selections/84 implementation comparisons and six verified fallback controls. Its earlier organ-pipe/p1 fallback hypothesis failed despite exact output checks; exact initial fixtures/source/result/diagnosis remain preserved, and the original initial full console stack remains an explicit missing artifact. Selection was changed to p95 before any measurement. No measured input was changed in response to the result.

Consolidation initially referenced `spec.samples` although the frozen manifest names its sample count `spec.n`. That assertion failed before producing a summary. The exact failed source and deterministic replay stderr are preserved in `recompute-attempt-1791843841504.*`; the corrected unmeasured authentication/arithmetic pass is `recompute-attempt-1791843863867.*`. The initial direct tool invocation's console error was not separately written to a raw file; the identical source failure was then captured by the controller before correction. This was a consolidation script error, not a measurement or candidate behavior failure. Preferred Matplotlib rendering failed because the bundled Python lacks that package; exact proposed source and replay stderr remain in `figure-attempt-1791844262530.*`, with the same direct-tool/replay distinction. Standard ReportLab SVG/PDF plotting then succeeded with source-bound summaries. SVG XML is parsed and all plotted range bounds checked, but no raster visual inspection was performed.

[Timing ranges](timing-ranges.svg) and [memory ranges with signed heap differences](memory-ranges-and-signed-deltas.svg) retain all displayed role ranges and signed paired values. PDF exports and the exact rendering/source digests are bound by [figure-validation.json](figure-validation.json). Figures are descriptive views of existing observations and execute no reducer or measured loops.

The source study inventory has **1,005 files**. This separate review preserves **1,003 exact source/log/fixture files, 11,263,497 bytes**. The two retained local original registry archives are excluded from public copying: `preserved/original/release.tgz`, 1,231,517 bytes, SHA-256 `954a03a68fa122ebe74c0c318dc801e434c17294c5374ef593cf491f73c81c41`; and `preserved/original/lodash-4.17.23.tgz`, 314,877 bytes, SHA-256 `9aba685f4b44d7a8e778cdf7085e9512143dabd78812df40e258375e1e8dceb4`. Their local identities remain authenticated in [study-preservation.json](study-preservation.json). The already excluded generated `.local/private-host-fixture` is not republished; its historical routing receipt preserves exact executed identities and confirms that an adjacent backend-only helper needs no public static-route change. The frozen original scripts/manifests contain this host's absolute paths; portable re-execution requires reconstructing those paths or a new, separately authenticated harness rather than silently editing this evidence.

Prospectively, the next independent algorithm stage should address selection pivot/work-budget behavior and fallback cost across the retained adversarial families, and examine shared multi-percentile overhead. It should keep these seven fixed evaluation inputs as historical controls and preserve standard arithmetic/cache/result identities, then pass full, held-out, alias, cache, fallback and work-cap correctness campaigns before seeking new measurement authorization. That is a next-stage proposal, not a tuned candidate, predicted speed improvement or accepted gate. Full-product completion, exhaustive correctness, universal superiority, performance parity and production integration remain false.
